==Restrictions==
Rarity: Only [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare]], [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare]] and [[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare]]

==Battleground==
*1 [[Aku Cyclone]] spawns as the boss after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*10 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*5 [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 30~36.67 seconds<sup>900f~1,100f</sup>.
*3 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*3 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*2 [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn after 146.67 seconds<sup>4,400f</sup>, delay 36.67~43.33 seconds<sup>1,100f~1,300f</sup>.
*3 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 180 seconds<sup>5,400f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 75% HP:
**3 [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn, delay 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.

==Strategy==
While this stage seems more difficult with the restrictions, many of the useful Cats for this stage can still be used. These include [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Aku Researcher]], who is now the main way of piercing Aku Cyclone's Shield. Due to the limited number of effective options and mediocre income within this stage, [[Cat Combo]]s, specifically Attack Up to kill the Aku Gories easier, are recommended. Players who have [[Ancient Egg: N109 (Rare Cat)|Barrel Cat]] can also use him to pierce Aku Cyclone's Shield even in the face of peons. [[Talents|Talented]] [[Matador Cat (Rare Cat)|Bellydance Cat]] also works well as a meatshield, though RNG is always at play. Generalist attackers such as [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] work well to clear the peons assuming high enough levels.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Evil Aku Researcher]] - This unit can be used to break the enemies in this stage's Shields but has low survivability, you can bring him along one more extra meatshield.
*[[Ancient Egg: N109 (Rare Cat)|Barrel Cat]] - Can instantly pierce enemy Shields within his effective range.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Matador Cat (Rare Cat)|Bellydance Cat]] - Has a good chance to dodge all damage inflicted by enemies in this stage, as well as a decent recharge speed.
*Talented [[Gardener Cat (Rare Cat)|Weedwacker Cat]] - Once the Aku Cyclone's Shield breaks, they are able to potentially lock it into a near-permanent Freeze until its next knockback. They are also able to assist in allowing other units to kill the Aku Gories.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] - Easily kills the Ginger Snaches in this stage and deal high damage generalist damage to other enemies.
*[[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]] - Their guaranteed ability to survive at least 2 hits invalidates Aku Gory's chance to perform a [[Savage Blow]] as it shall die quickly either way.
*Talented [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] - Her Survive Talent allows her to serve as a secondary meatshield along with generally being a strong Area Attacker.


==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Most [[UBERFEST (Gacha Event)|UBERFEST]] units work well here, as their abilities towards traited can help inflict high amounts of damage at a time when shields are broken.
*[[Netherworld Nymph Lunacia (Uber Rare Cat)|Netherworld Nymph Lunacia]] - Can help pierce the Shield of all Aku enemies present from a safe range. Also Weakens Aku, improving the survivability of all your units.
*[[Kaoru Hanayama (Uber Rare Cat)|Kaoru Hanayama CC]] - With Shield Piercing, he can deal massive amounts of damage at a time and can tank hits from the Aku enemies (besides Aku Cyclone) in this stage.
*[[Hevijak the Wicked (Uber Rare Cat)|Wicked King Hevijak]] - Wielding a 50% chance Pierce Shields, being Reisistant to Aku, and having Knockback against every enemy in this stage, Hevijak can be a great help for keeping the Cyclone at bay, as well as assisting your units by piercing the Shield of said enemies if your primary Shield Piercers don't.
*[[White Knight Cyclops (Uber Rare Cat)|White Knight Cyclops/Black Knight Cyclops]] - Either form of this unit can be used, but the first is used for crowd control and Piercing Shields in general, while the second form is used damage from a safe distance, but does not Pierce Shields, which means you will still need other piercers.

